\par\par \b \uc2  Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2 / \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -2:  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Reserves Stable \b0\par\par\uc2 141 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 1997\par 07:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-Dow Jones)--Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Soedradjad Djiwandono said Tuesday that Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent roughly $1 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rupiah in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets over the past week. \par \par \uc2  Soedradjad added that all of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was done in the forward markets. As a result, there could be no depletion to Bank Indonesia's foreign reserves, provided the rupiah continues to strengthen. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia first came into the market with the rupiah trading at an all-time low of 2,662.50 rupiah/U.S. dollar July 22. So far Tuesday, the U.S. dollar has fallen to 2,575.50 rupiah, after closing Monday at 2,898 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  At the end of May, Bank Indonesia had roughly $21 billion in reserves. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0557GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7t05k8w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
