\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Rupiah seen weakening further in short term. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Raju Gopalakrishnan \par \uc2 560 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, July 24 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah, which has been volatile after plunging to a record low against the dollar on Monday, is likely to weaken in the short-term despite the country's strong economic fundamentals, economists said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  They said problems in rolling over corporate debt and contagion from weakness in several regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should push the rupiah toward the lower end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. \par \par \uc2  "I still think we are still firmly in an environment of dollar strength against the regionals," said Desmond Supple, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  specialist at BZW Asia in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "Over the short-term, I would expect to see convergence of spot rupiah and the weaker end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. While fundamentally this weakness is not justified, this contagion continues to ensure that the perceptions of fundamentals are more important than the fundamentals themselves." \par \par \uc2  The rupiah opened in Jakarta at 2,575/85 against the dollar on Thursday and by late evening was trading at 2,613 in the spot market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  posted its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band at 2,378/2,682. \par \par \uc2  It crashed to a historic low of 2,665 against the dollar on Monday after becoming the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fall victim to speculative attacks which have plagued the region. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  brought about a partial recovery on that day, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been extremely volatile with swings between 2,530 and 2,625 since then. \par \par \uc2  Traders say although the rate has not fallen out of the band, Bank Indonesia, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has pumped some $700 million into the market. \par \par \uc2  But they add that regional fallout, especially from the Thai baht, has made those efforts apparently futile. \par \par \uc2  UBS Research said in a report that markets would take some time to assess the differences between the fundamentals of the Indonesian and Thai economies. \par \par \uc2  "The baht was attacked because of the perception that the rigid exchange rate regime was inconsistent with sharply dropping economic activity and high domestic interest rates," it said. \par \par \uc2  "Conditions are different in Indonesia, which has a much more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  system, robust economic activity and ample liquidity in the financial system." \par \par \uc2  But the report cautioned that rupiah weakness would persist for the next three to six months, at least partly because of problems in Indonesian corporate debt. \par \par \uc2  "There is evidence that more Indonesian corporates are facing difficulties in rolling over their maturing foreign liabilities," UBS said, pointing to higher risk premiums and possibly lower credit limits because of falling investor confidence in nations with large current account deficits. \par \par \uc2  "As a result, more Indonesian corporates will have to buy rupiah and convert into foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  domestically," it said. "Unless supported by strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , this will add pressure to the rupiah." \par \par \uc2  Over the longer-term, analysts and dealers said 2,550 was fair value for the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  "At the 2,550 level, that's really comfortable," said an analyst with a U.S. bank in Singapore, adding that many fund managers were looking to sell dollars above the 2,600 level. \par \par \uc2  Others said the longer-term view was that strong exports in the second half of the year should bolster the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which would then recover to a four-to-five percent guided depreciation trend. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7o024io\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
