\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah/Amplifier -2: Domestic Hedging Drives Mkt \b0\par\par\uc2 429 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 1997\par 14:24\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Indonesian companies with large foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  borrowings or that have large import requirements would be most exposed to the rupiah's plunge. Local banks or financial institutions were also hedging against a rupiah drop. \par \par \uc2  'There was a tremendous amount of hedging going on in Indonesia,' said a Singapore-based \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  director at a major European bank. 'And as often the case, if a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is going to break it will happen from domestic forces. The power of hedge funds is limited.' \par \par \uc2  Analysts say they are unsure to what extent major Indonesian corporates are hedged, but Monday's action suggests many still needed to put such protection in place. \par \par \uc2  The action was also reflected in swap rates. Although rupiah liquidity remained adequate at the short end, swap rates rose substantially in the longer tenors as Indonesian banks sought to cover their short dollar positions, both in the spot market and through forwards. U.S. dollar/rupiah one-month swap rates rose to 35/40 rupiah late Monday from 20/24 rupiah early in the day. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was sighted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - even though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has indicated previously it would only need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the limits of the trading band. \par \par \uc2  One local trader said he was receiving rupiah buy orders from Bank Indonesia at 2,650 rupiah/dollar, while another said he received orders to buy rupiah in the three-month and six-month forward markets. Bank Indonesia didn't, however, resort to significantly increasing its money-market rates. \par \par \uc2  Despite the potential threat to its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading band, analysts said Bank Indonesia's move earlier this month to widen the rupiah trading band - in the midst of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turmoil elsewhere in Asia - has been shown as farsighted. \par \par \uc2  By pre-emptively widening its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading band to 12% from the previous 8%, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  avoided the need to spend billions of dollars defending the rupiah - since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move Monday would have burst the limits of the old 8% band. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at $21 billion at the end of May, good for 5.6 months of imports. Though that's healthy in comparison with the Philippines, recent events have shown that speculative attacks can quickly push reserve levels down to unacceptable levels. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand, with reserves of more than $30 billion, was forced to abandon its defense of the baht earlier this month. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 21-07-97 \par \par \uc2  1224GMT \par \par \uc2  1135 62555 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7l05bqw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
