\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Plunge Puts Cntrl Bk In Dilemma: Amplifier \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jay Solomon \par \uc2 381 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 1997\par 13:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-Dow Jones)--Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's relative isolation from Southeast Asia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turmoil ended abruptly Monday with a wicked 5.7% plunge in the rupiah, its steepest one-day fall ever. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah's fall buffeted Jakarta's stock market, with the key market index closing 1.6% lower, and is forcing financial analysts to re-evaluate Indonesia's economic prospects. And with the weak end of the rupiah's trading band now less than 40 rupiah away, Bank Indonesia is now grappling with the same dilemma already faced by its humbled Asean neighbors - whether to draw a line in the sand and try to stop a further weakening in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Many \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts doubt that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be able to defend its present \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band for long. \par \par \uc2  'Bank Indonesia said it would defend the rupiah (at the weak end of the band), but this probably isn't sustainable,' said Rajeev Malik, regional economist at Jardine Fleming in Singapore. 'Either they will have to widen the band again, or possibly not announce a new band but still allow the rupiah to fall to a speculative attack.' \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  set its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band Monday at 2,378 rupiah to 2,682 rupiah. Malik said Bank Indonesia could possibly widen the band to as much as 20% from its current level of 12%. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's rise Monday was fast and furious, jumping more than 100 rupiah to an Asian close of 2,645 rupiah, up from 2,510 rupiah at the close Friday. The rupiah weakened as far as 2,662.50 rupiah per dollar Monday, a drop of 5.7%, before reports of Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  caused it to rebound from its lows. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah has now fallen nearly 12% since the beginning of the year, well above Bank Indonesia's 'managed depreciation' target of 4%-5%. \par \par \uc2  But unlike selling pressures on the rupiah last week - said largely to be from offshore speculators - Monday's fall came largely from domestic players, dealers said. Panicked with the prospects of accumlating massive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses, locals move quickly to cover their rupiah exposure. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 21-07-97 \par \par \uc2  1137GMT \par \par \uc2  1135 62555 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7l05bkg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
