\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah weakens on dollar short-covering. \b0\par\par\uc2 448 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, July 16 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah weakened against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on short-covering in dollars in moderate early trading on Wednesday , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  One U.S. bank dealer said the rupiah strengthened at the opening to 2,453 from 2,455 and the New York closing of 2,458/59, but slid back to 2,457/78 at 0225 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "I think it's a combination of dollar short-covering ahead of Thursday's public holiday and ample liquidity," the dealer said, adding volume was relatively high. \par \par \uc2  All markets will be closed on Thursday for the birthday of Prophet Muhammad and reopen on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trading was not as dramatic as Monday, but the market remained edgy on on-going volatility in the region. \par \par \uc2  They said operators were not fully comfortable and remained cautious of a possible spillover if sentiment changed. \par \par \uc2  However, one Japanese bank dealer said spreads were narrowing, suggesting improved confidence in the market. \par \par \uc2  "There is good demand from both local and foreign side but supply is also sufficient. People don't want to be caught too long or too short if other markets turn naughty on Thursday," another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Tomorrow and today rupiah were at 2,455.25/56.50 and 2,454.75/56.00, respectively. \par \par \uc2  Liquidity was ample for now, with overnight rates traded at around 8.0/9.0 percent in the morning. Overnight swap was at 0.3/0.4 and tom/next at 0.6/0.7 points. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. bank dealer said swap rates were edging up after easing at the opening, suggesting some volatility remained. \par \par \uc2  But he said local operators were taking profits on foreign selling, limiting sharp declines in swap premiums. \par \par \uc2  Offshore operators had stocked up rupiah with swaps previously to prepare for a possible squeeze by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fend off speculation. \par \par \uc2  But the bank had pursued an unchanged monetary policy, generating arbitrage opportunity for local players with cheap rupiah funds to fill foreign appetite for swaps. \par \par \uc2  "Now local players are cashing out and limited a quick adjustment in swap rates," one Japanese bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He said offshore operators had to lift swap prices higher before they could unload their positions, otherwise the losses were too large. \par \par \uc2  One-month swap was at 18.0/20.0, two at 37.0/40.0, three at 55.0/59.0 and six at 105/1.09 points. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band by one point to 2,376/2,680 but lowered the conversion band to 2,425/2,473 on Tuesday -- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7g02lfm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
