\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah stable as swaps up slightly. \b0\par\par\uc2 411 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, July 15 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah was stable against the dollar in calmer late trading on Tuesday but swap premiums edged up on offshore purchases, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  One Japanese bank dealer said the market was calmer as offshore players re-entering the longer-term swap market. \par \par \uc2  "Some are looking for good levels to sell the dollar. I think the rupiah could stage a gradual recovery when the regional markets calm down," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "But some offshore players are buying longer-term swaps, causing rates to increase slightly from early lows," he said. \par \par \uc2  But the dealer said some offshore players might have to boost swap rates because they were too long in the swap market. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think they can cut their heavy long positions now. They have to raise them to higher levels before they could sell. Otherwise the losses are too large," he said. \par \par \uc2  One local bank dealer said local players were seen delivering the amounts needed by those offshore because they could make good profits out of arbitrage from the money market. \par \par \uc2  He said money market rates were so low that local players could fill the offshore appetite for swaps. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money fell to six percent from 15 percent in the morning. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered bilateral overnight papers (SBIs) at six percent, one-week at seven percent, two at 8.25, one-month at 10.25, three- at 10.50, six and 12-month at 11.25 and 12.00 percent, respectively. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was at 2,450.5/51.5 at 1000 GMT, compared with an opening of 2,455.0/65.0. Tomorrow and today rupiah closed at 2,450.0/1.0 and 2,446.5/47.5, respectively. \par \par \uc2  Overnight swap was at 0.38/0.40 and tom/next at 0.5/0.6. \par \par \uc2  Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were still edgy, but traders said volatility in the markets appeared to be slowing down. \par \par \uc2  One-month swap edged up to 18.0/20.0 from 16.0/20.0, two to 33.0/40.0 from 30.0/35.0, three to 58.0/62.0 from 50.0/55.0 and six to 108/112 from 102/105 points. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band by one point to 2,376/2,680 but lowered the conversion band to 2,425/2,473 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7f02jmh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
