\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS - Indonesia rupiah recovers after early hits. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mantik Kusjanto \par \uc2 661 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 1997\par 12:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, July 14 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah recovered against the dollar after being sent on a roller-coaster ride by speculative attacks on other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the rupiah was not a direct target of fund managers but was affected by the attacks on the Malaysian ringgit and the Philippine peso. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah bounced back to 2,450 a dollar at the Jakarta close from an intra-day low of 2,469.0 per dollar on Monday morning. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah opened at 2,453.0 and recovered to 2,445.0 before succumbing to fresh selling pressure. \par \par \uc2  "For the rupiah, the issue is definitely the spillover from the peso and the ringgit," Edwin Png, country treasurer of Bank of America, told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "It's not because of the fundamentals of the rupiah," he said, adding that fund managers were taking advantage of Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements. \par \par \uc2  "They want to buy it up as high as possible. But the rupiah situation is not that bad because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  only widened the band last week," Png said. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , surprised the market on Friday by widening the dollar-rupiah band to 12 percent from eight percent following recent de facto devaluations of the Philippine peso and the Thai baht. \par \par \uc2  The move helped the rupiah briefly strengthen to 2,410.0 on Friday but it later surrendered ground again, closing at 2,438.0 to the dollar as speculators maintained their assault on regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Friday's widening was the eighth since 1992. The bank set its band at 2,375-2,679 rupiah to the dollar on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has widened the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band in steps to give more room for price fluctuations to absorb external and internal shocks. \par \par \uc2  "They are smart to do that. Fortunately, they didn't let it float like the peso and just widened the band," Png said, adding a float could have a wider impact on the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  However, economists remained comfortable with the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Daragh Maher, an economist at ING Barings, said earlier any effect on the rupiah due to a spillover from other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be short-lived. \par \par \uc2  He said stable economic growth, the long-term nature of the country's foreign debt and controllable short-term private debt were among the factors helping to shield the rupiah from speculation. \par \par \uc2  Kobus van der Waht, regional treasury economist at Standard Chartered Bank in Singapore, told Reuters Financial Television the band widening was a pre-emptive move. \par \par \uc2  "Bank Indonesia doesn't want to be part, or doesn't want to be in the same trap as happened in Thailand and to an extent in the Phillippines over recent weeks or months," he said. \par \par \uc2  "Taking pre-emptive action (on band) and saying the past policy of depreciation is very much intact. \par \par \uc2  "Decision making is over to the market and there is not going to be a situation where a specific level is defended at the cost of losing very valuable reserves," van der Waht said. \par \par \uc2  Png said the top side of the dollar was expected to be at the 2,470 level because of overseas selling interest. \par \par \uc2  "If you take the depreciation, it's very small compared to other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. He added the turbulence could last for a couple of weeks but was confident of Bank Indonesia's ability to handle the situation. \par \par \uc2  "I think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is very well prepared compared to other central banks. They are more controlled in the sense that for the past 12 months the rupiah was always under attack." \par \par \uc2  "The market is somehow already used to that. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is already used to that, unlike others," Png said. \par \par \uc2  "Somehow the economy is not really out of hand. I think they are doing a good job so far to control the economy and also the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement." \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7e02q1w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
