\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia/Afiff -2: In Tokyo For Consultative Group Meeting \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mia Nielsen \par \uc2 228 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 1997\par 06:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-Dow Jones)--Indonesia's top economic minister said Monday that Thailand's decision to float the baht isn't a major concern for Indonesia's rupiah or its economy. \par \par \uc2  Saleh Afiff, coordinating minister for economy, finance and development supervision, told Dow Jones in an interview that Thailand's recent move 'is not worrisome'. \par \par \uc2  Afiff, who is in Tokyo for the July 17 meeting of the Consultative Group on Indonesia, a group of international aid donors, also said Indonesia wouldn't take any action on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless speculators hit the ceiling or floor of the rupiah's new band. \par \par \uc2  'As long as they don't hit the ceiling, Indonesia won't do anything. As long as they don't hit the floor, Indonesia won't do anything,' the minister said. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia Friday widened its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band in which the rupiah can float against the dollar before \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 12% from 8%. This created a floor of 2,374 rupiah and a ceiling of 2,678 rupiah. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band was last widened September 11, 1996. \par \par \uc2  At 0350 GMT (11:50 p.m. EDT), the dollar is trading at 2,452.50 rupiah, down from an intraday high of 2,467.50. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0403GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7e0537b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
