\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia/Rupiah Calm -2: Proactive Economic Policies \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 1997\par 13:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band has been widened in stages from as little as 2% in late 1995. Despite a slew of political shocks in the interim - such as rioting in the capital last year and concerns over President Suharto's health - the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been able to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  comfortably within the band. Usually it has traded near the stronger end. \par \par \uc2  'When traders look at the rupiah, they see it at the strong end of the band, with 8% downside, that's a lot of risk' for a speculator, Belchere said. 'No one is willing to bet on that.' \par \par \uc2  The same kind of prompt action has been seen on the economic policy front. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand resisted floating the baht because of fears of the effects a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation would have on the financial sector, already suffering from excessive lending to the depressed property sector. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia, in contrast, has been much more proactive in stemming excessive property speculation and in limiting offshore borrowing by Indonesian companies - though economists concede that some pressures remain. \par \par \uc2  In response to growing concerns over property lending, Bank Indonesia Monday put a moratorium on lending to property companies engaged in land purchases or land development. And Bank Indonesia Governor Soedradjad Djiwandono said Wednesday that the country's tight monetary policies will remain in place. \par \par \uc2  That has helped Indonesia avoid the kind of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility, and the need for regular market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , that has been seen in Malaysia, for example. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stated policy of depreciating the rupiah by about 5% per year allows investors to know exactly where the market is headed. \par \par \uc2  'It's normally a severe punishment when Bank Negara (Malaysia) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market - they always do it aggressively and market participants get bruised,' said Pardi Kendy, head of the treasury at PT Bank Buana Indonesia. 'It's the opposite script in Indonesia. The rupiah is very stable and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has never been harsh to market players.' \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-07-97 \par \par \uc2  1116GMT \par \par \uc2  1145 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7a052oa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
