\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Calm Amid Sea Of  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Speculation \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jay Solomon and I Made Sentana \par \uc2 369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 1997\par 12:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-Dow Jones)--Amid a wave of speculative attacks on the neighboring \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Thailand, Malaysia, and the Philippines during the past few months, the Indonesian rupiah has enjoyed a pleasant respite. \par \par \uc2  As the Thai baht has plunged in the wake of Thailand's July 2 decision to float the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , both the Malaysian and Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have come under renewed attack, prompting \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and interest rate hikes to defend them. \par \par \uc2  But Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has been able to stay on the sidelines. A chart of the dollar/rupiah rate since early June is more or less flat - a period of extreme turbulence in the other Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Indeed, with the dollar currently at 2,431.23 rupiah, the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is very close to the strongest level it can reach within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current trading band of 2,430 to 2,622 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  The reason? Strong economic fundamentals, for one, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders say, as well as prompt steps by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to head off worries about economic overheating. But maybe even more important has been Bank Indonesia's well-timed moves to widen the rupiah's trading band and thus take a less prominent role in guiding the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's day-to-day movements. \par \par \uc2  'Indonesia has listened to its advisors and instituted some extremely prudent moves regarding its exchange rate mechanism,' said Bill Belchere, head of fixed-income research at Merrill Lynch & Co. in Singapore. 'At 8%, they now have one of the most flexible exchange rate systems in the region, which has put them in extremely strong position.' \par \par \uc2  The trading band was widened to 8% in September, from the previous 5%. \par \par \uc2  There has been some speculation recently that the band will be widened further, though many economists say that's unlikely since it would probably only encourage further rupiah strength. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a policy of depreciating the rupiah by around 5% annually in order to encourage non-oil exports. So far this year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fallen 2.8%. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-07-97 \par \par \uc2  1059GMT \par \par \uc2  1145 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7a052jc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
