\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah stable after Thai shock. \b0\par\par\uc2 585 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, July 2 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah was stable against the dollar in late trading on Wednesday after the market recovered from an early shock generated by turmoil in the baht. \par \par \uc2  Thailand set a fresh \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy on Wednesday by letting its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  float against the dollar, prompting a slew of baht selling and sending jitters through the region. \par \par \uc2  However, the rupiah emerged unscathed from the turbulence, staging a strong comeback with an upward trend. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market shrugged off a possible spillover effect as economists hailed strong fundamentals shown by the country's latest macroeconomic indicators. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah, due next Monday following a public holiday in the United States on Friday, was quoted at 2,433.0/33.25 against the dollar at 0900 GMT, compared with an opening of 2,432.5/33.5. The rupiah tumbled to a low of 2,445 on selling by offshore players on rumours of a baht devaluation. It recovered after Thailand announced its managed float policy. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the Indonesian economy was stronger than that of Thailand, with the country enjoying a healthy trade surplus, sufficient \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, a manageable current account deficit, low inflation and an eight-percent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. \par \par \uc2  They said those indicators helped the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to comfortably absorb external shocks and internal uncertainty induced during the May general elections. \par \par \uc2  "I am quite surprised how well the rupiah held up," said Daragh Maher, an economist at ING Barings, adding that previous pressures on the rupiah were election-related. \par \par \uc2  "Over the last two to three months when other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region were under a lot of pressure by virtue of the baht, actually the pressure we have seen on the rupiah had been more election-related," Maher said. \par \par \uc2  He said with the election out of the way people were more comfortable with rupiah risk and that helped explain the relatively strong rupiah performance. \par \par \uc2  Economists said the rupiah might gradually drift towards the strong end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band when the Thai baht settles. \par \par \uc2  One U.S. bank dealer said there was also speculation in the market of a possible dollar-rupiah band widening ahead of the Consultative Group for Indonesia (CGI) donor meeting in Tokyo later this month. \par \par \uc2  The World Bank, which coordinates the CGI, said in a report on \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month that some countries had a wider \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band but did not specifically suggest that Jakarta follow suit. \par \par \uc2  But \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sudradjad Djiwandono said it was not good sense to follow what other people were doing. \par \par \uc2  "This kind of argument is weak. That is not good economic policy that just because other poeple have 15 percent we have to go to 15 percent," Djiwandono said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rupiah remained firm, also shrugging off excess rupiah supply in the money market. Overnight rates fell to four percent from 11.0/12.0 percent in the morning. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said overnight dollars had also stabilised to six percent. Tomorrow and today rupiah closed at 2,432.00/32.35 and 2,433.5/34.00, respectively. \par \par \uc2  One-month swaps were at 12.0/13.0, two at 26.5/27.5, three at 38.0/39.0 and six at 79.0/81.0 points. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band at 2,427/2,619 and the conversion band at 2,427/2,475 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7202zyy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
