\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah eases in late trade, swaps down. \b0\par\par\uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, July 1 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah was soft in late trading on Tuesday in face of continued ample liquidity and a stronger dollar against the Japanese yen and other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The rupiah remained under pressure because of continued ample liquidity and a stronger dollar against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," one European bank dealer said \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was at 2,432.00/32.50 at 1005 GMT against an opening of 2,431.80/32.30. \par \par \uc2  Tomorrow and today rupiah were last at 2,432.00/32.50 and 2,433.00/33.50, respectively. \par \par \uc2  Another foreign bank dealer said reports on Indonesia's expected June consumer price index did not have much impact on the market as the figure was still within expectations. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's consumer price index for June was likely to show a month-on-month fall of 0.16-0.18 percent, compared with a rise of 0.19 percent in May, government officials said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Short-term swaps also remained under pressure from the strong dollar and sustained ample rupiah liquidity, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  One senior director with a U.S. bank in Jakarta said the falls in the rupiah short-dated swap rates were due to rising onshore dollar lending rates because of quarter and half-year end demand. \par \par \uc2  "As a result dealers who need to borrow US$ overnight and tom/next have been generating them by buying and selling US$ through the short-date swap market," the director said. \par \par \uc2  Overnight swap was last at -0.10/par from an opening of 0.15/0.30 while tom/next was down at -0.05/par against 0.10/0.20 at the opening. \par \par \uc2  One-month swaps also fell to 10.50/11.00 from an opening of 11.00/12.00, two fell to 22.50/24.00 from 25.50/26.50, three to 37.00/38.00 from 36.25/37.25 and six to 77.50/79.00 from 81.00/82.50 points. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , raised its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band by one point to 2,427/2,619 and its conversion band also by one point to 2,427/2,475 late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt71036gs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
