\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Won't Widen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Band Soon \b0\par\par\uc2  By Vito J. Racanelli \par \uc2 320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 1997\par 06:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WASHINGTON (AP-Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to widen the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band for the rupiah in response to the recent steady depreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to Bank Indonesia governor Soedradjad Djiwandono. \par \par \uc2  In an interview with Dow Jones last week, Soedradjad countered recent market speculation that rupiah weakness could give the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  room to expand its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, currently 8%. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts argue the rupiah weakness gives the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  a window of opportunity to widen the band, without triggering the capital inflows and rupiah appreciation that accompanied the band widenings last year. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is well on track to achieve its policy of depreciating the rupiah by 3-5% annually, in order to help the country's non-oil exports. That may give it room to widen the band still further, some analysts say. \par \par \uc2  But Soedradjad says that isn't the case. \par \par \uc2  'I don't want to rock the boat when things are working. I know that this has been the concern of the markets,' Soedradjad said. \par \par \uc2  Interviewed in Washington during the spring meetings of the International Monetary Fund and the World Bank, Soedradjad emphasized that he is happy with the rupiah's band as things stand. \par \par \uc2  Just because the rupiah has already fallen substantially in 1997, it doesn't mean that 'we have to jump now' to widen the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, Soedradjad said. 'It's not as mechanistic as that,' the governor added. \par \par \uc2  The dollar started 1997 at 2,365.00 rupiah but has risen to trade at 2,427.75 rupiah at present, a rupiah depreciation of around 2.6% and somewhat faster than the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band for the rupiah is currently set between 2,407 to 2,599 rupiah per dollar. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 06-05-97 \par \par \uc2  0425GMT \par \par \uc2  1137 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt56039lx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
