\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah remains firm in late trading. \b0\par\par\uc2 428 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, April 28 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah remained firm against the dollar in late trading on Monday as fears over campaign violence calmed down, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said a relatively expensive overnight rate was also keeping operators cautious as the month-end approached. \par \par \uc2  "I expected the rupiah to recover today but not in a 10-point magnitude. It's a surprise," one Japanese bank dealer said, adding that the tight market was also not factored in. \par \par \uc2  He said the tight rupiah market had played a major role in cooling down the dollar. Overnight rupiah rose to 14.0 percent from 10.5 percent in the morning. \par \par \uc2  Overnight swap ended at 0.60/0.65 points. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah rose to a high of 2,426.5 before settling at 2,426.5/27.0 at 0915 GMT from an opening of 2,435.5/36.5. \par \par \uc2  Tomorrow and today rupiah closed at 2,426.0/26.5 and 2,429.5/30.0. respectively. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese bank dealer said he expected the rupiah to remain steady on Tuesday, with operators keeping an eye out for further developments on the streets. The campaigning period will last to May 23 for the general elections on May 29. \par \par \uc2  The campaign on Tuesday proceeded without any major reports of incidents after a smooth start on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  Saleh Aziz, treasury manager of PT Bank Export Import Indonesia, said the rupiah was expected to recover gradually if things remained under control. \par \par \uc2  "I think the rupiah will go back to the bid side of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) band and people will start to focus on the liquidity issue again," Aziz said. \par \par \uc2  Aziz said it would be difficult for the dollar to touch the 2,440 level again, broken last week after the market factored in possible disruption during the campaign. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the relatively expensive rupiah on Monday was also attributable to dollar purchases last week which needed to be financed with the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Japanese bank dealer said longer-term swap rates were little changed while rupiah financing for the dollar buying was done through short-term swaps. \par \par \uc2  One-month swap was at 12.0/13.0, two at 25.25/26.00, three at 37.25/38.0 and six at 74.25/74.25 points. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band by two points to 2,406/2,598 but lowered the conversion band by seven points to 2,406/2,454 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4s06fsa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
