\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah weakens in late trading. \b0\par\par\uc2 571 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, April 23 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah weakened against the dollar late on Wednesday on high liquidity and worries over the coming election campaign, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  One U.S. bank dealer said reports of a strike by some 10,000 workers under contract to Nike Inc and flush rupiah supply in the afternoon boosted sentiment on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Some 10,000 of the 13,000 workers at a factory under contract to Nike marched from their plant in Tangerang on Jakarta's outskirts to the local parliament on Tuesday to demand a wage increase. They were granted a pay rise after staging a mass strike and protest, Antara news agency reported. \par \par \uc2  "The tone is still biddish on the dollar. But there is a lot of fight at the 2,420 level," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said ample rupiah liquidity also helped dollar purchasing. One local bank dealer expected more upside for the dollar after it broke through the 2,420 resistance level several times. Spot rupiah was at 2,420.00/20.25 at 0930 GMT after fluctuating between the 2,417.0 and 2,421.0 range. \par \par \uc2  One \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer in Singapore said the tone seemed to be biddish on the dollar, with the brief response to the Nike demonstration reflecting only general caution ahead of the campaign starting on Sunday for the May 29 elections. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah strengthened briefly in the morning following a report in a local daily quoting a university professor and an unnamed official as saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was planning a band widening in the near future. But the report was later ignored by the market as operators switched focus to politics. \par \par \uc2  A noted economist said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to widen its band in the short- or medium-term because there was no fundamental reason to back it up at present. \par \par \uc2  "The rate is hovering at a healthy level below the mid-rate of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band and moderately higher than the floor rate. I don't see any reason to act now," the economist said. \par \par \uc2  He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had implemented a new reserve rate of five percent only last Wednesday which should help contain money supply growth, which exceeded targets in 1996. \par \par \uc2  The economist said there was no immediate reason to act and the effect of the new reserve rate had to be disgested first. \par \par \uc2  "Political issues are taking the lead for now. People are worried over possible riots and things like that as we enter the campaign period," the Singapore dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Tomorrow and today rupiah closed at 2,419.40/19.80 and 2,416.5/17.0, respectively. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money fell to 9.5 percent in the afternoon from 13.0 percent. Overnight swaps were at 0.45/0.50 points. \par \par \uc2  Tom/next were at 0.40/0.42 points. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said swap premiums were little changed from the opening after fluctuating in narrow-range trading. \par \par \uc2  They said the focus was on the spot market. \par \par \uc2  One-month swaps were at 11.5/12.5, two at 23.0/23.5, three at 33.75/34.75 and six at 71.5/72.5 points. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band by one point to 2,404/2,596 and the conversion band at 2,404/2,452 on Wednesday. -- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4n06q5f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
