\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah stable in range trading. \b0\par\par\uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, April 23 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah was stable against the dollar in range trading on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said volume was thin in the morning, with some players seen trying to cash out from spot dollars on the back of relatively expensive tom/next swaps. \par \par \uc2  One U.S. bank dealer said spot rupiah ended at 2,419 in New York overnight, triggering operators to cash out in Singapore and Jakarta as tom/next was traded at 0.40/0.45 points. \par \par \uc2  He said operators were worried over prospects of a tightening after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market policy was neutral on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said liquidity was not really tight. Overnight money eased down to 11.5 percent from 12.0/13.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The underlying sentiment remains biddish for the dollar despite some early profit-taking after sharp dollar increases on Tuesday," the U.S. bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He said the dollar was expected to hover between 2,417 and 2,418 in the morning. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was at 2,417.25/17.75 at 0200 GMT, compared with an opening of 2,418.5/19.5. Tomorrow and today rupiah were at 2,416.75/17.25 and 2,416.5/17.0, respectively. \par \par \uc2  One state bank dealer said the rupiah was engineered down late on Tuesday on liquidity and political factors. \par \par \uc2  He said the approaching general elections on May 29 would keep the tone biddish on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, the rupiah might be supported in the short-term due to month-end factors. \par \par \uc2  Overnight swap was at 0.4/0.5 points. Another dealer said swap rates inched up slightly following an easing in overnight money, but were sold off later by offshore players. \par \par \uc2  One-month swaps were at 11.5/12.0, two at 22.5/24.0, three at 34.0/34.5 and six at 71.75/72.75 points. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band by one point to 2,403/2,595 and the conversion band at 2,403/2,451 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4n06puu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
