\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah weakens on dollar short-covering. \b0\par\par\uc2 412 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, April 17 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah weakened against the dollar in late trading on Thursday following some short-covering in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "I think it's mainly short-covering which is driving the dollar higher. We haven't heard anythin yet in the market," one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer in Singapore said, adding some dollar buying at the London opening helped push the rate up further. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah fell to 2,412.0/12.5 at 0840 GMT from an opening of 2,407.75/08.75. Tomorrow and today rupiah closed at 2,411.75/12.25 and 2,407.75/08.50, respectively. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the sudden dollar upturn was not linked to a small protest by supporters of ousted minority party leader Megawati Sukarnoputri as there was no violence. \par \par \uc2  About 100 supporters of Megawati marched one km from the office of her chief lawyer to the Central Jakarta State Court to lodge a lawsuit against her ouster. \par \par \uc2  One local bank dealer said excess rupiah supply in the afternoon seemed to have aided increased dollar buying. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money dropped to seven percent from 14.0 percent at the opening. \par \par \uc2  "Operators tend to go slightly long over the extended weekend. They just want to play safe," the dealer said. The market will be closed on Friday for a public holiday. \par \par \uc2  He said short-covering by both local and foreign players boosted the dollar and sustained a bullish dollar tone. \par \par \uc2  "Sentiment now appears to be bullish on the dollar. It might proceed until the election," another said. Indonesia will hold general elections on May 29. \par \par \uc2  Dealers were cautious in the morning, one day after a new bank reserve requirement rate of five percent was made effective. \par \par \uc2  But the market appeared to be flush on ample \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  supply and on adequate anticipation by banks. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced the new requirement last year. \par \par \uc2  Tom/next swap was at 0.20/0.23, down from 0.28/0.33. \par \par \uc2  Dalers said swap rates edged up slightly in the afternoon. \par \par \uc2  One-month swaps were at 11.50/11.75, two at 24.0/25.0, three at 35.5/36.5 and six at 71.5/72.5 points. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band by one point to 2,402/2,594 and the conversion band to 2,402/2,450 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4h06xu2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
