\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah softens, swaps ease on liquidity. \b0\par\par\uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, April 15 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah softened against the dollar and swap rates also declined in early trading on Tuesday on the back of ample liquidity, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The market is liquidity-driven. Operators are a little bit surprised by the ample conditions," a local bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said operators seemed to be well prepared to face the new bank reserve requirement rate on Wednesday, helped by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  injection of 847 billion rupiah on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  One \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer in Singapore said trading in the spot market was dull and added the focus was on the swap market. \par \par \uc2  "The first reaction on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  supply was forward selling. People think it might be the same again tomorrow, so they started selling in response," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He said six-month swaps fell to 71.5 from 74.0, but expecting strong support at the 70.0 level. "I don't have a clear view for the market at present. But I would buy on dips." \par \par \uc2  The dealer said declines in short-term swaps were also caused by some weakening in one-to-five-year swaps. \par \par \uc2  The local bank dealer said spot rupiah rose to a high 2,403.80 from an opening of 2,403.75/04.25 before softening to 2,405.0/05.2 at 0300 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Tomorrow and today rupiah were at 2,404.0/04.5 and 2,403.75/04.25, respectively. \par \par \uc2  Overnight swap edged down to 0.15/0.25 from 0.45/0.50 and tom/next to 0.38/0.43 from 0.48/0.50 points. \par \par \uc2  One Japanese bank dealer said offshore players were seen buying back at low levels after they initiated early selling. \par \par \uc2  One-month swaps were at 12.5/13.5, two at 24.5/26.5, three at 36.0/38.0 and six at 71.0/73.0 points. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band by one point to 2,400/2,592 and the conversion band to 2,400/2,448 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4f072eu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
