\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah firms on liquidity concerns. \b0\par\par\uc2 452 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, March 25 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah firmed against the dollar in active late trading on Tuesday on concerns over money market conditions, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the money market was fluctuating throughout the day, keeping the dollar-rupiah rate volatile. \par \par \uc2  One U.S. bank dealer said the dollar rebounded briefly at midday as liquidity was ample, but fell in the afternoon on rises in the overnight rate. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was last at 2,397.25/97.75 at 0930 GMT after having fallen to the 2,340 level from a high of 2,397.0. It opened at 2,401.0/02.0 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Tomorrow and today rupiah closed at 2,396.75/97.50 and 2,398.50/99.25, respectively. Tom/next was at 0.45/0.60. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money rose to 21.0 percent after easing to 12.0/12.5 percent at midday. Dealers said higher tax payments at the end of the 1996/97 fiscal year were the main cause. \par \par \uc2  "The market is mainly liquidity-driven," one said. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said some players wanted to link the dollar selling to a possible band widening by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  but they seemed to have failed to drive the market to follow. \par \par \uc2  "Liquidity is the main issue. We have only two more days to settle all the outstanding taxes," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The market will be closed on Friday for a public holiday and Monday for the fiscal year-end and reopen on April 1. \par \par \uc2  "Operators are bullish on the rupiah at present. But they are alert if market sentiment turns around when liquidity conditions change," the U.S. bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Swap rates continued to edge up as the rupiah remained well bid in the wake of the fiscal year-end. \par \par \uc2  One-month swaps rose to 12.0/12.5 from 10.5/11.5, two to 24.0/25.0 from 22.5/24.0, three to 35.0/36.0 from 34.0/35.0 and six to 70.5/72.0 from 69.0/70.0 points. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band by one point on Tuesday to 2,392/2,584 and the conversion band to 2,392/2,440. \par \par \uc2  One foreign bank dealer said earlier a possible rate hike in the United States had only marginal impact on the market. \par \par \uc2  "The focus is on liquidity. A possible hike seems to have been widely discounted," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "Besides, this is positive in the sense that it would narrow interest rate differentials between the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and help curb recent heavy capital inflows," he added. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt3p08962\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
