\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah stable after discount rate cut. \b0\par\par\uc2 435 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, March 12 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah was stable against the dollar in moderate early trading on Wednesday following a cut in a key discount rate, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The cut surprised the market but many operators had already expected the discount rate cut to take place in February or March after a cut in December," one state bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia on Wednesday cut its key discount rates for short-term securities (SBPUs) by 50 basis points for all maturities. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was generally stable and was last quoted at 2,395.75/96.25 at 0340 GMT from 2,395.80/96.80 at the opening. \par \par \uc2  One-week SBPUs fell to 14.75 percent, two to 15.0 percent, and one month to 15.50 percent. \par \par \uc2  SBPUs are papers purchased by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to inject liquidity into the banking system. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said the discount rate cut had been expected following recent declines in rates of SBIs (securities issued by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to absorb liquidity). \par \par \uc2  "The cut has been expected after months of generally ample rupiah liquidity and declines in SBI rates" another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  One Japanese bank dealer said the discount rate cut did not have an immediate impact on the rupiah as it was generally stable. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the SBPU cut was seen as a signal from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that interest rates were expected to be on the downward trend in the future. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  director C. Harinowo told Reuters Financial Television on Wednesday that the discount rate cut decision was based on an improved outlook inflation in Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rate cut, however, was not likely to push the rupiah further down, as demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected to strengthen ahead of financial year reporting session in late March. \par \par \uc2  Tomorrow and today rupiah were at 2,395.50/96.25 and 2,395.25/95.75 respectively. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rupiah was expected to remain little changed on Wednesday, with spot rate seen moving in the range between 2,395.50 to 2,397.00. \par \par \uc2  Overnight swap was last quoted at 0.20/0.25 and tom/next at 0.10/0.20. \par \par \uc2  One-month swaps was last quoted at 9.50/10.25, two at 22.00/22.75, three at 35.0/36.50 and six at 74.0/74.75 points. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band at 2,386/2,578 and the conversion band at 2,386/2,434 late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt3c08s61\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
