\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia's Rupiah -2: 1.511 Tln Rupiah Injected \b0\par\par\uc2 164 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 1997\par 04:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia, the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , injected a large amount of 1.511 trillion rupiah in net liquidity into the money market early Friday. \par \par \uc2  The expiration of Sertifikat Bank Indonesia (SBI), Bank Indonesia's short-term notes, added 1.571 trillion rupiah to the system. However, the expiration of Surat Berharga Pasar Uang (SBPU), money market's certificates, absorbed 20 billion rupiah out, in addition to 40 billion rupiah through the settlement of new SBIs. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia's Governor, Soedradjad Djiwandono, reiterated late Friday that the current ample liquidity of the rupiah is only seasonal in anticipation of a high demand for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  toward the end of the fiscal year and the increase of the statutory minimum reserve requirement to 5% from 3% April 16. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  early Friday left its dollar-rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band at 2,381 rupiah-2,573 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 28-02-97 \par \par \uc2  0336GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt2s01f8i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
