\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Up Vs. Dlr On Central Bk Widening Rumors \b0\par\par\uc2 224 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 1997\par 05:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-Dow Jones)--Indonesia's rupiah is up versus the U.S. dollar in trading early Wednesday, driven higher by market rumors that Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was moving to widen its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. \par \par \uc2  The rumors have not been substantiated, however, and many dealers have already discounted them. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. unit is being bought at 2,388 rupiah in the spot market at 0307 GMT Wednesday, after starting the day at 2,388.50 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell all the way down to 2,385.54 rupiah on the spot market at 0035 GMT on the widening rumors before stabilizing later in the day. \par \par \uc2  'The rupiah definitely received a boost from the widening rumors, but I don't give them any credence at all,' said Trisiladi Supriyanto, a dealer at Bank of America in Jakarta. 'I don't see the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  making any move until after the general elections.' \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's elections are set for May. \par \par \uc2  Despite discounting these rumors, dealers still expect the market to continue to be choppy through the rest of Wednesday. Dealers now see the dollar trading in a range between 2,386 rupiah and 2,390 rupiah through the rest of Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 26-02-97 \par \par \uc2  0417GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt2q018f6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
