\par\par \b \uc2  ASIAN EXOTICS - Dollar firms against regionals. \b0\par\par\uc2 593 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Feb 13 (Reuter) - The greenback maintains its firm tone against most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at midday on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit was marginally higher on fresh buying against the Singapore dollar but continued strength in the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped gains, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Lots of people are looking to cover their short (dollar) positions because dollar/majors are strong," said the head of dealing at a foreign bank in Malaysia. \par \par \uc2  He said the market was still thin and choppy as many dealers were still away after the holidays for Chinese Lunar New Year and Moslem Eid al-Fitr festivals. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market would return to normal next week when the ringgit was expected to make fresh gains. \par \par \uc2  At 0400 GMT, the ringgit was at 2.4838/48 a dollar and at 1.7504/7523 a Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said technical ringgit buying after 1.7513 level broke had brought down ringgit/Sing further. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said ringgit was expected to continue appreciating against the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht slipped below 26.00 to the dollar in early trade after the Bank of Thailand set the midrate at a new six and a half year low of 25.98. \par \par \uc2  Its bid/offer were at 26.003/010 a dollar at 0400 GMT against 25.990-25.995 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "There still seems to be bidding interest (for the baht) at the moment. Though it is trading at the top of the range the market appears normal and not overly active," said a Bangkok-based trader at a US bank. \par \par \uc2  The one month baht/dollar swap premium fell to 11.50/12.50 satangs per dollar against 14.00/15.00 late on Wednesday due to improved liquidity, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah edged lower against the dollar on the back of relatively ample supply in moderate early trading. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said anticipation of additional liquidity supply from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday helped ease short-term swaps, which enabled short-term money market rates to decline. \par \par \uc2  They said overnight money had been kept at relatively expensive levels in the past few days despite sufficient supply due to arbitrage chances between the swap and money markets. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers said the gap was narrowing after broad anticipation of fresh rupiah supply on Friday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to support the dollar on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was at 2,378.50/9.50 at 0400 GMT against an opening of 2,378.0/79.0. Tomorrow and today rupiah were at 2,376.75/77.50 and 2,376.25/76.75, respectively. \par \par \uc2  Swap premiums were lower but dealers were cautious on longer-term swaps due to the new reserve requirement rate of five percent which will become effective on April 16. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band by one point to 2,377/2,569 and the conversion band to 2,377/2,425 on Wednesday, the first depreciation this week after four points last week. \par \par \uc2  Singapore dollar held steady against the dollar. The market shrugged off Singapore's finance minister Richard Hu comments that there was no need to take special steps to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had fallen to a six-month low against the US dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was at 1.4180/90 to a dollar at 0400 GMT. \par \par \uc2  -- Madhav Reddy in KL (603-230 8911), Mantik Kusjanto in Jakarta (6221-384-6364), Anuchit Nguyen in Bangkok (662) 652-0642 and Angela Tan in Singapore (65-8703083) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dt2d00cz8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
