\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Steady Vs U.S. Dlr Late; Tight Liquidity \b0\par\par\uc2 173 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 1997\par 10:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-Dow Jones)--Indonesia's rupiah has remained vitually flat against the U.S. dollar in moderate dealings late Monday as tightened liquidity ahead of the month-end continues to spark interest in rupiah, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened at 2,374.62 rupiah in the spot market Monday and was trading just a tad lower at 2,372.37 rupiah at 0246 GMT (9:46 p.m. EST). The dollar, however, weakned slightly to trade at 2,372.20 rupiah at 0924 GMT (4:24 a.m. EST) late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile on the swap market, short-dated swaps strengthed slightly through the course of Monday. The premium of the overnight swap was slightly higher at 0.50 rupiah from 0.45 rupiah, earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , kept its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band stable at 2,369 rupiah to 2,561 rupiah late Monday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 27-01-97 \par \par \uc2  0953GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1r00men\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
