\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah weakens on ample liquidity. \b0\par\par\uc2 423 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Jan 23 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah weakened against the dollar in volatile early trading on Thursday on the back of excess rupiah supply, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But some foreign bank dealers said there could be a light spillover from early turbulence in the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  categorically denied rumours in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market that the baht might be devalued. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think it's the spillover from Thailand because dollar buyers are mainly from Jakarta centre," one dealer in Singapore said, which was confirmed by Jakarta dealers. \par \par \uc2  One local bank dealer said operators were seen moving into dollars following excess rupiah supply domestically. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said ample liquidity pushed short-term swaps down, driving interest rates in the money market to follow. \par \par \uc2  Overnight swaps fell to 0.10/0.15 from 0.25/0.35 points and three-day tom/next swaps to 0.7/0.8 from 1.00/1.15. \par \par \uc2  "The market this morning is mainly liquidity-driven. There seems to be some fresh government transfers for civil servants' 13th month salaries," another local bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The payment was linked to the upcoming Eid al-Fitr celebration on February 9 and 10. \par \par \uc2  Overnight rupiah was last traded at 7.5/8.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said sentiment on the dollar appeared to be bullish at present, triggering some operators to go long on dollars. \par \par \uc2  The local bank dealer said declining swaps trend might encourage some players to go long as the dollar downside was limited by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said earlier diminishing speculation for a band widening could be supportive for long positions, but the market needed relatively stable short-term swap rates. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was at 2,373.25/74.00 at 0315 GMT, compared with an opening of 2,371.25/71.75. \par \par \uc2  Tomorrow and today rupiah were at 2,372.75/73.25 and 2,372.75/73.25, respectively. \par \par \uc2  The local bank dealer said, however, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixing policy needed to be watched as it had depreciated the rupiah by only one point so far against four points last week. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band at 2,368.0/2.560 and the conversion band at 2,368/2,416 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  One-month swaps were at 11.25/11.75, two at 21.00/22.50, three at 33.25/34.25 and six at 71.00/72.00 points. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt1n02c7g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
