\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Slightly Dn Vs. Dlr Late: Lack Of News \b0\par\par\uc2 165 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 1997\par 11:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-Dow Jones)--Indonesia's rupiah is slightly weaker against the U.S. dollar in quiet dealings late Tuesday as most players chose to stick to the sidelines due to a lack of fresh incentives, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar, which opened at 2,370.37 rupiah on the spot market Tuesday, traded at 2,370.52 rupiah at 0255 GMT before strengthening to 2,371.15 rupiah at 0934 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Dealers noted that Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , kept its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band steady at 2,368 rupiah to 2,560 rupiah. The narrowing of the spot level with the lower end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, dealers note, could have pushed the dollar slightly higher in afternoon trading. \par \par \uc2  Activity was also quiet in the swap market, but sentiment remains bullish on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the short-term swaps, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 21-01-97 \par \par \uc2  1000GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1l00euz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
