\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  defies rumours of rupiah band change. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mantik Kusjanto \par \uc2 654 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1997\par 11:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Jan 13 (Reuter) - Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to defy foreign speculation on a widening of the rupiah's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band and snapped up dollars to keep the rupiah from rising too high, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Offshore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  operators had bought rupiah on Friday, speculating that a widening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band was imminent. Past widenings of the band had caused the rupiah to appreciate sharply. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the speculation continued on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "It's less vigorous than Friday, but enough to maintain upward momentum for the rupiah," one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said. \par \par \uc2  At 0850 GMT, spot rupiah fall back slightly to 2364.40/5.40, after opening on Monday at 2,363.75/64.10. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band by one point late on Monday to 2,364/2,556. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band is an optimal rupiah-dollar exchange range set daily by the bank. If the rupiah rises or falls out of the band, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable. \par \par \uc2  The band has become the market focus since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  widened its band to eight percent from five percent last September. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers in Jakarta said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was estimated to have absorbed at least $1.1 billion last Friday to keep the rupiah from rising out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. \par \par \uc2  They said the impact was felt in the market, with swap premiums tumbling across the board on expectation of ample rupiah liquidity on Tuesday induced by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar-buying. \par \par \uc2  Swap rates are premiums which allow operators to roll over positions established in the cash market. \par \par \uc2  One local bank dealer said offshore operators were still challenging the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday to widen its band after they failed last Friday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sudradjad Djiwandono shrugged off market speculation last week by saying monetary policy would be kept flexible and adjusted whenever necessary. \par \par \uc2  However, he also said the rupiah exchange rate would be kept at a realistic level without anti-export bias. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there were rumours in the market that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might try to teach speculators a lesson by tightening the allocation of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  papers (SBIs) this week. \par \par \uc2  SBIs are \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  instruments used to tighten liquidity in the money market and are also options for offshore investors to park their funds temporarily. \par \par \uc2  "If the rumours come true, people with ample rupiah might be squeezed if they haven't placed their rupiah yet. Interbank rates this morning have given the signals," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He said he doubted offshore operators had found alternate rupiah investments, which may result in further roll-overs of existing short dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  "This is a tug-of-war. I don't know how long they can hold. They are now being squeezed on the swap side," he added. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said some offshore operators appeared to have given up for now, which was reflected in the dollar's slight recovery since Friday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar dropped three points below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band last Friday on heavy band speculation. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said offshore operators might be forced to buy back dollars if they started to calculate the value of their speculation. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said offshore operators were seen mainly sustaining short dollar positions as reflected in declining tom/next swap rates, which were traded below par levels. \par \par \uc2  "If they can't find adequate rupiah investments and cannot get out of the swap market, they will buy back," another said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said offshore operators seemed to be trying to launch another attack on the band by spreading rumours of a band widening on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  They said Wednesday was selected as the day because some players usually went short on dollars on Wednesdays and bought them back on Thursdays to enjoy weekend rupiah premiums. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt1d06e9p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
