\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah ends 1996 on stable note. \b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Dec 30 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah was stable against the dollar on Monday, the year's last trading day, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the dollar-rupiah rate closed at 2,362.0/62.5 on Monday, against an opening of 2,363.0/64.25. It compared with an opening of 2,281.0/83.0 on January 2 this year. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was barely any volume, with trading limited to position squaring and to some customer orders. \par \par \uc2  Tomorrow and today rupiah closed at 2,361.50/62.50 and 2,363.75/64.25, respectively. One dealer said sentiment on the rupiah stayed firm despite ample liquidity in the money market. \par \par \uc2  He said offshore operators were still speculating on a band widening by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and some expected it to come in the first quarter of next year. He said this might explain the sustained pressure on dollars. \par \par \uc2  Swap premiums remained cheap on ample rupiah supply. Overnight swap was at -0.25/par and tom/next at 0.27/0.30. \par \par \uc2  Overnight dollar deposit rate settled at 7.5 percent after rising to a high of 12.0 percent at midday on tight supply. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money closed at 7.5 percent after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered three-day papers (SBIs) at seven percent. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will be closed on December 31 and January 1. It will resume trading on January 2. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate by one point to 2,359/2,551 and the conversion rate to 2,359/2,407 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia fixing 