\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah jolted briefly on riot news. \b0\par\par\uc2 471 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Dezember 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Dec 27 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah was jolted briefly against the dollar in early trading on Friday following riots in the west Java town of Tasikmalaya, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said Singapore operators were seen trying to push the dollar up but met resistance from local operators. \par \par \uc2  "Singapore operators made spot reaction at the opening but were countered by local players. Offshore players seemed to feel strong local resistance and cut losses," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The dealer, for a U.S. bank, said spot rupiah fell briefly to 2,364.5 before recovering to around the opening level. \par \par \uc2  One local bank dealer said some local and state banks were seen capping the dollar from any upturn. \par \par \uc2  He said reaction was brief only because the riots were confined to Tasikmalaya and had not spread. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was quoted at 2,363.0/63.5 at 0250 GMT against an opening of 2,362.0/63.0. Tomorrow and today rupiah were at 2,362.5/63.0 and 2,362.25/62.50, respectively. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said ample rupiah supply in the money market also aided some weakening of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, the local bank dealer said overall sentiment on the rupiah remained firm despite excess supply. \par \par \uc2  "I think players are still speculating for a band widening. They remember previous \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves at year-end," he said. \par \par \uc2  Residents of Tasikmalaya said a crowd of several thousand people ran amok apparently after police had beaten a religious school teacher and his two students on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  They said the mob set fire to churches, shops, commercial buildings and vehicles. Tasikmalaya was quiet but tense on Friday morning, with the military reporting at least two dead. \par \par \uc2  Witnesses said the rioters had targeted ethnic Chinese businesses, and also burned down at least two Christian churches in the town of some 500,000 people. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said year-end factor seemed to have helped prevent a more drastic reaction in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "People do not want to take up fresh positions at year-end. They mainly stayed squared despite the news," one said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will be closed on December 31 and January 1. It will reopen on January 2. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said swap rates remained soft on ample rupiah supply. Overnight swap due Monday was at 0.2/0.3. \par \par \uc2  Tom/next swap was quoted at 0.53/0.56 points. \par \par \uc2  One-month swaps was at 13.70/14.40, two at 28.00/29.00, three at 41.5/42.5 and six at 84.50/86.50 points. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate by one point to 2,358/2,550 and the conversion rate to 2,358/2,406 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019dscr01r28\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
