\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah stable in slow late trading. \b0\par\par\uc2 425 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Dezember 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Dec 27 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah was stable against the dollar in late trading on Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said trading was dull, with operators seen shrugging off the Thursday riots in the west Java town of Tasikmalaya. \par \par \uc2  One Japanese bank dealer said operators were mainly staying on the sidelines amid excess rupiah supply in the money market. \par \par \uc2  "There is no drive in the market. People are just waiting for the day to pass. They don't want to take any initiative at this time of the year," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market would be even quieter on Monday, the year's last trading day. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will be closed on December 31 and January 1, and reopens on January 2. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was at 2,363.3/63.5 at 0900 GMT against an opening of 2,362.0/63.0. Tomorrow and today rupiah closed at 2,363.10/63.35 and 2,362.25/62.50, respectively. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was briefly jolted in the morning due to news of the riots, but it managed to recover quickly to the opening level from the day's low of 2,364.5 on local support. \par \par \uc2  They said the Tasikmalaya riots were unlike riots in the past, when operators responded swiftly with rupiah selling. \par \par \uc2  One foreign bank dealer said the absence of offshore operators due to the holiday season helped prevent any drastic response in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  He said reaction was brief because the riots did not spread to other places. \par \par \uc2  Residents of Tasikmalaya said a crowd of several thousand people ran amok apparently after police had allegedly beaten religious school teachers. \par \par \uc2  They said the mob set fire to churches, shops, commercial buildings and vehicles. A military official said at least two people had died in the rioting. \par \par \uc2  Hundreds of troops patrolled the riot-torn town on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said sentiment on the rupiah remained firm, with many operators still watching the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. \par \par \uc2  They said swap rates remained soft on ample liquidity. \par \par \uc2  Overnight swap was at 0.2/0.3 and tom/next at 0.4/0.5. \par \par \uc2  One-month swaps was at 14.00/14.25, two at 28.00/29.00, three at 41.1/42.5 and six at 84.50/86.50 points. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate at 2,358/2,550 and the conversion rate to 2,358/2,406 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019dscr01qpu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
