\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah little changed in late trading. \b0\par\par\uc2 255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Dec 12 (Reuter) - Indonesia's rupiah was little changed against the dollar in slow late trading on Thursday, with tom/next swaps rising ahead of an expected liquidity tightening on Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The tom/next swap rate was higher in active trading as operators expect liquidity to tighten on Friday due to likely large tax payments," one Japanese bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The dealer, however, said the spot rate barely moved and was trapped in a narrow range. \par \par \uc2  "The chances of an upward movement in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, have been restricted by earlier expectations of a higher \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixing in the afternoon," another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band by one point to 2,351/2,543 and the conversion band to 2,351/2,399 late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was last quoted at 2,352.75/53.20 against an opening of 2,352.50/53.25. \par \par \uc2  Tomorrow and today rupiah were last quoted at 2,351.00/51.30 and 2,350.50/50.90, respectively. \par \par \uc2  Overnight swap was at 0.35/0.45 from an opening of 0.45/0.55 while tom/next was last at 1.70/1.80 against an opening of 1.60/1.70. \par \par \uc2  One-month swap was at 15.00/15.75, two at 30.50/31.50, three at 43.00/43.75 and 12 months at 170.00/175.00 points. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019dscc02dom\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
