\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Up Vs Dlr Ahead Of Year-End Tax Payment \b0\par\par\uc2 234 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 1996\par 03:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-Dow Jones)--Indonesia's rupiah strengthened slightly against the U.S. dollar in fairly active trading early Wednesday as banks loaded up on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of year-end tax payment, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar, which opened at 2,352 rupiah Wednesday, was trading at 2,351.62 rupiah in the spot market at 0215 GMT. The dollar closed Tuesday at 2,352.87 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trading was also active in the swap dealings especially for overnight, and three-day settlement. The premium of the overnight swap rose to 0.45 rupiah from 0.35 rupiah, meanwhile the premium of the three-day swap increased to 1.8 rupiah from 1.5 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  'Companies are getting prepared to pay year-end tax next week,' said Trisiladi Supriyanto, a dealer with Bank of America in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  Dealers see rupiah's bullishness reigning the market this week and see the dollar tied up at its support level of 2,351 rupiah through Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers don't expect Bank Indonesia, the nation \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to increase the dollar-rupiah trading band again later in the day after increasing it for two days in a row. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band was 2,350 rupiah - 2,542 rupiah early Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 11-12-96 \par \par \uc2  0235GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011014dscb01p9z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal