\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia/Dlr-Rupiah Trading Band -3: Aware Of Rumor \b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 1996\par 12:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Speaking at a seminar, Soedradjad added that he is aware of the rumor being spread around the market that Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will widen the band soon. \par \par \uc2  'It's the game that financial analysts and players are playing now,' he stated. He added that such a rumor has made some players confused and suffer losses. \par \par \uc2  'But that's the nature of the game: someone's gain is other people's loss. What we want is for someone's gain not to be Bank Indonesia's loss,' he said. \par \par \uc2  Soedradjad, however, said that Bank Indonesia will widen the band again when it thinks it is necessary. 'We are not going to do that if we think it isn't necessary yet,' he stated. \par \par \uc2  Soedradjad outlined that one of the purposes of widening the dollar-rupiah trading band is to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves from the volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past when the dollar was trading beyond the trading band. It had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling the dollar three times last year when the dollar traded above the upper-end of the trading band. \par \par \uc2  At that time, the spread of the trading band was only 44 rupiah. The first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in January 1995 following the crisis of Mexico's peso. The second \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in April 1995 as the yen's sharp rise against the U.S. dollar was seen inflating Indonesia's foreign debt. The third one was in August 1995 when the rupiah was attacked by unfounded devaluation rumors. \par \par \uc2  But so far this year, Soedradjad said Bank Indonesia has not had to sell the dollar to the market, thanks to a wider trading band. He said such an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not necessary although the rupiah was under great pressure against the dollar in July following news of President Suharto's health and political riots in Jakarta on July 27. At that time, the spread of the trading band was 116 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 03-12-96 \par \par \uc2  1123GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011014dsc301etn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
