\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia says  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  band widening helps debt. \b0\par\par\uc2 153 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Nov 26 (Reuter) - Indonesian Finance Minister Mar'ie Muhammad said on Tuesday the widening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-rupiah trading band was positive for foreign debt payments. \par \par \uc2  "The strengthening of the rupiah does not put a burden on our principal and interest debt payments. The effect was instead positive because we only need less rupiah to repay debts," Mar'ie told parliament. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  widened its dollar-rupiah trading band, or so-called \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, to eight percent in September from five percent. This band allows the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the rate falls outside its limits. \par \par \uc2  The band widening had caused the rupiah to strengthen sharply against the dollar in the past. \par \par \uc2  The World Bank has previously said Indonesia's foreign debt stands at about $100 billion. \par \par \uc2  - Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019dsbq02xxt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
