\par\par \b \uc2  ASIAN EXOTICS - Regionals ease on dollar strength. \b0\par\par\uc2 744 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 November 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  * Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  under pressure from dollar rise versus majors after news of Italy's re-entry into Exchange Rate Mechanism. \par \par \uc2  * Indonesian rupiah eases on ample liquidity, with upward pressure seen. Support pegged at 2,344/45 and resistance at 2,347/48. \par \par \uc2  * Baht hit by firmer dollar/majors. Support seen at 23.443/44. \par \par \uc2  * Malaysian ringgit eases on heavy dollar/mark buying by U.S. funds. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Nov 25 (Reuter) - Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were hit by the dollar's gains against the majors on Monday after news of Italy's re-entry into the Exchange Rate Mechanism (ERM). \par \par \uc2  In Indonesia, dealers said ample liquidity also weighed on the rupiah, causing players to buy the dollar and sell forward swaps down. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah fell to 2,346.00/47.00 at 0450 GMT from the open of 2,343.50/44.50 on sustained bullish dollar sentiment. \par \par \uc2  Overnight swap declined to 0.22/0.26 from 0.25/0.35 points on flush money market liquidity, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  One local bank dealer in Jakarta said cheap local funds continued to sustain further buying interest in the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The buying is seen driven mainly by local operators, which forces offshore operators to reduce short dollar positions," he said, adding that the momentum was still prevalent. \par \par \uc2  "We are now some points above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. There is more room to trade now. We believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not widen the band in the medium-term," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  One economist said earlier the present \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation policy suggested that it did not plan to widen its band in the medium-term. \par \par \uc2  Offshore operators had been putting pressure by going short on the dollar, triggering speculation of another band widening by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the back of heavy capital inflows. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been resisting the pressure and had even challenged the market. \par \par \uc2  The local bank dealer said he would maintain a long dollar position as long as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintained its three- to four point rupiah depreciation each week. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said operators were also seen buying dollars in anticipation of narrowing interest rate differentials between the dollar and the rupiah after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seemed to loosen its monetary policy recently. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate by one point to 2,340/2,532 and the conversion rate to 2,340/2,388 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  In Thailand, concern over the new finance ministry post weighed on the baht. It was quoted at 25.443-25.447 to the dollar at 0450 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said dollar/baht was likely to be dictated by the dollar/majors, mainly the dollar/mark after mark/lira weakened on Italy's re-entry into the ERM. \par \par \uc2  They said the market ignored the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor's call on banks to cut their minimum loan rates to boost the economy, but instead focused on the new cabinet lineup. Activity was also driven by this month's reserve requirement. \par \par \uc2  "Banks began to keep funds for the next reserve requirement. The interbank rate is likely to stand above 10 percent this week," said one dealer at a foreign bank in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  "I think the market is expecting liquidity to tighten due to the maintenance period and this is supporting the six month-forward rate at the 44/45 level," a Singapore dealer said. \par \par \uc2  In Malaysia, the ringgit broke out of its recent range to head south on heavy dollar/mark buying in early Tokyo, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the ringgit was just tracking the trend in major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and was likely to ease further. \par \par \uc2  "There is too much pressure. It is hard to be short dollar this morning," said a dealer with a U.S. bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar faced resistance at the 2.5220 level, which if broken, could see the ringgit falling to 2.5280. \par \par \uc2  "Ringgit is expected to retreat for a while, if not today, in the next few days. So it is a good opportunity to buy dollars at any dip," a dealer with a Kuala Lumpur bank said. \par \par \uc2  At 0450 GMT, the ringgit was at 2.5235/45 to the dollar against 2.5194/04 late on Friday. \par \par \uc2  -- Madhav Reddy in Kuala Lumpur (603-230 8911), Mantik Kusjanto in Jakarta (6221-384-6364), Anuchit Nguyen in Bangkok (662-652-0642) and Angela Tan in Singapore (65-8703080) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019dsbp035hc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
