\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Flat Vs. Dlr; Central Bk Raising Band \b0\par\par\uc2 263 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 1996\par 04:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-Dow Jones)--Indonesia's rupiah is flat versus the U.S. dollar in sluggish trading early Wednesday on mixed sentiment, dealers said. The Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to remain in an extremely tight range of between 2,338 rupiah and 2,339 rupiah through the rest of Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is moving to weaken the rupiah by continuing to gradually increase the lower end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, dealers note. Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  increased the lower end by one rupiah Tuesday to 2,338 rupiah, and is expected to increase the band by one rupiah more Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The upside for the dollar, however, is capped by continued strong interest in the rupiah, market players said. The rupiah's high yield, as well as demand for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the Monday listing of state-owned PT Bank Negara Indonesia, are all seen keeping the rupiah firm. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. unit is being bought at 2,338.52 rupiah in the spot market at 0254 GMT Wednesday, after starting the day at 2,338.50 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  'The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is eager to keep hot money out of the system,' said Pardi Kandy, a dealer at Bank of America. 'By keeping the market extremely liquid in rupiah and raising the lower end of the band, they're moving to ward speculators off.' \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia early Wednesday injected another 468 billion rupiah into the money market system, dealers said, keeping the market liquid. \par \par \uc2 