\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah stable in slow late trading. \b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Oktober 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Oct 17 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah was stable against the dollar in slow late trading on Thursday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its fixing rate unchanged. \par \par \uc2  "Players were waiting for another suprise on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fixing policy this afternoon, but it has kept the rate unchanged," one Japanase bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said the policy to keep the rate unchanged had kept the rupiah moving in a narrow range. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia surprised the market on Wednesday by raising its fixing for the second day in a row, suggesting it was serious about challenging players who wanted to test the band. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said relatively ample rupiah liquidity in the market also kept the rupiah within a narrow trading range. \par \par \uc2  They said spot rupiah was last quoted at 2,323.20/23.50 against an opening of 2,323.00/24.00. \par \par \uc2  Rupiah liquidity on Friday, however, was unlikely to be as ample as on Thursday due to expected corporate tax payments and large SBPU maturities, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  One European bank dealer said sharp rises in the tom/next swap rate on Thursday reflected a higher demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Tom/next swap rose to 2.10/2.30 from 1.60/1.70. Overnight swap was last at 0.10/0.30 against an opening of 0.30/0.40. \par \par \uc2  One-month swap was quoted at 17.5/18.5, two at 35.50/36.0, three at 52.0/53.0 and six at 103.0/104.0 points. \par \par \uc2  The local bank dealer said the dollar-rupiah rate was expected to range between 2,323.0 and 2,324.5 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The cental bank, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , maintained its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate at 2,322.00/2,514.00 and the conversion rate. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018dsah01r2x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
