\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah stable, focus on liquidity. \b0\par\par\uc2 706 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Oct 10 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah was stable against the dollar in moderate late trading on Thursday, with operators seen focusing on Friday liquidity, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The market still seems to be nervous over Friday liquidity conditions," one Japanese bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He said operators were wary about possible carry-forward effects of tight conditions from previous Fridays although the impact was seen diminishing last Friday. \par \par \uc2  However, the fears and the fact that Friday was the last day to improve banks' positions ahead of the next liquidity report on October 15 caused short-dated swaps to rise, he said. \par \par \uc2  "It's a good chance to arbitrage," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said focus was on tom/next swap rate which rose to 3.50/3.70 points from 2.75/3.0 points at the opening. \par \par \uc2  Overnight swap closed at 0.55/0.65 points. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said rupiah supply in the money market was not that tight but the market was driven up mainly by rising swap rates. "Major players are still short in the forward market. They are taking short-dated swaps to cover positions. Friday would be the last chance to improve off-balance sheet positions," one said. \par \par \uc2  But the Japanese bank dealer said interbank rates may ease on Friday if major players could square off on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money fell to 10.0 percent from 14.0/15.0 percent in the morning, one local bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "It seems people here are speculating for a tight Friday. I just got hit (on tom/next swap) all the way up," he said, adding that both local and offshore players were present. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese bank dealer said some operators seemed to be caught by the off-balance sheet limitations which forced them to take up swaps instead of cheaper rates in the money market. \par \par \uc2  Tom/next rupiah was quoted at 16.5 percent, compared with the equivalent of tom/next swap at around 18.76 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said expensive short-dated swap rates continued to cause some adjustments in longer-term swap premiums. \par \par \uc2  One-month swap edged up to 19.50/20.00 from 18.5/19.5, two to 36.50/37.50 from 35.0/36.5, three to 53.50/54.50 from 53.0/55.0 and six to 103.0/104.5 from 102.5/104.5 points. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said offshore players were still speculating for a band widening but the view was not shared by local operators as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had just widened its band last September. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese bank dealer said offshore pressure to test the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's band seemed to have eased in the afternoon. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar offers were immediately off from brokers' boxes after knowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has raised the fixing by one point. This may indicate that offshore players didn't want to proceed with the challenge for today," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Offshore operators started testing the band late on Wednesday, raising the rupiah out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ceiling after the official squaring time at 0900 GMT. \par \par \uc2  However, the rupiah had returned to within the parameters of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band this morning. State bank dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was quoted at 2,320.5/20.60 at 0945 GMT against an opening of 2,320.50/21.00. Tomorrow and today rupiah closed at 2,317.00/17.35 and 2,316.25/16.75, respectively. \par \par \uc2  One U.S. bank dealer said earlier offshore players were trying to create reasons to sell dollars and also to challenge the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  One \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer in Singapore said offshore players were heavily short on dollars. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think Bank Indonesia would give in to offshore pressure," the U.S. bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would widen its band again at present," one economist attached to a state bank said. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate by one point to 2,320/2,512 and the conversion rate also by one point to 2,320/2,368 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018dsaa01z87\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
