\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah firms, swaps up in late trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Oct 8 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah firmed against the dollar in slow late trading on Tuesday as swap rates were seen edging up further, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said overall trading was slow but some dollar selling from Singapore operators seemed have brought the rate closer to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's floor rate. \par \par \uc2  One U.S. bank dealer said there were some big orders to sell dollars from Singapore in the afternoon but the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was well supported at the 2,321.25 level. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was quoted at 2,321.0/21.5 at 0845 GMT against an opening of 2,322.5/23.00. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trading was in a narrow-range but some profit taking on dollars helped limit any further downside. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. bank dealer said the selling of dollars might be due to preparations for weekend payments. \par \par \uc2  Tomorrow and today rupiah closed at 2,320.30/20.90 and 2,320.25/20.75, respectively. \par \par \uc2  He said expensive short-dated swaps, possibly on worry over liquidity outlook, had driven longer-term rates up. Overnight swap was at 0.65/0.70 and tom/next at 0.70/0.80 points. \par \par \uc2  "The swap market seemed to neglect liquidity condition. We have sufficient rupiah but swaps remained high." he said. \par \par \uc2  One local bank dealer said swaps covering by joint-venture and foreign banks appeared to have driven short-dated swaps up. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said high swaps had also forced offshore operators to cut long dollars positions. \par \par \uc2  One-month swap rose to 20.25/20.50 from 19.0/20.0, two to 35.5/37.0 from 34.50/35.25, three to 53.5/55.0 from 52.25/53.50 and six to 103.50/104.75 from 102.0/104.0 points. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate at 2,318/2,510 and the conversion rate at 2,318/2,366 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018dsa80244n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
