\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Up Vs. Dlr Due To Liquidity Concerns \b0\par\par\uc2 219 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 1996\par 06:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-Dow Jones)--Indonesia's rupiah is strengthening versus the U.S. dollar in trading early Thursday as tightened liquidity is driving up demand for the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. unit is being bought at 2,323.50 rupiah in the spot market at 0419 GMT Thursday, after starting the day at 2,325.25 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Traders see the dollar trading in a range between 2,322 rupiah and 2,325.50 rupiah through the rest of Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers note that the dollar had been gaining ground following comments earlier in the week by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Soedradjad Djiwandono that a further widening of Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading band wouldn't occur in the near-term. As the dollar had been trading down near the lower-end of the band, dealers used the news to start driving the dollar higher. \par \par \uc2  Currently, the Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has set its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band at 2,317 rupiah - 2,509 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  'The dollar started out quite strong at the 2,325 rupiah level but liquidity concerns have driven it back down,' stated Trisiladi Supriyanto, a dealer at Bank of America. 'I don't see liquidity being restored until next week.' \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 03-10-96 \par \par \uc2  0440GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013dsa307y93\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
