\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah little changed in sluggish trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 557 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Sept 24 (Reuter) - Indonesia's rupiah was little changed against the dollar in sluggish late trading on Tuesday ahead of the U.S. Federal Reserve policy meeting, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  One major local bank dealer said trading was pretty quiet, with operators reluctant to take the initiative due to the month-end factor and the U.S. Federal Open Market Committe (FOMC) meeting later on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "The market has been really dull in the past two days. I don't expect much at present," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He said operators' focus now was on liquidity, which was seen as much more important than the U.S. interest rates. \par \par \uc2  "If the Federal Reserve hikes rates by 0.25 percentage point, there won't be much effect on the market. The main issue for us now is liquidity," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  But one U.S. bank dealer said earlier there could be some portfolio adjustments if it were a 0.5 percentage point raise. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market seemed to have factored in a 0.25 percentage point rise in interest rates by the Federal Reserve. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was last at 2,318.25/18.75 at 0900 GMT against an opening of 2,318.5/19.5. One Japanese bank dealer said some short-covering of dollars was seen late in the afternoon but strong support for the rupiah persisted. \par \par \uc2  "There was no change in sentiment on the rupiah. It would still be traded around the ceiling," one said. \par \par \uc2  He expected the dollar-rupiah rate to range between 2,318.0 and 2,320.0 on Wednesday. Tomorrow and today rupiah closed at 2,317.70/18.00 and 2,317.75/18.00, respectively. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese bank dealer said overnight money was last traded at 9.5 percent, with a stable outlook seen for Wednesday as Tuesday's excess supply was placed in overnight papers (SBIs) offered by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at nine percent. \par \par \uc2  "I'm not so worried about liquidity supply until Thursday but people are worrying over a possible repeat of tight conditions on Friday," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Jakarta's interbank market was hit by tight rupiah supply in the last two Fridays, causing operators to cash in one-week papers for temporary liquidity, but with a carry-forward effect. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the impact might have subsided but banks remained cautious due to the month-end factor. \par \par \uc2  Overnight swap was at 0.25/0.35. Tom/next swap rate eased to 0.45/0.50 from 0.52/0.55 points on ample liquidity. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said longer-term swap rates were stable. \par \par \uc2  They said earlier players seemed to make some deals in anticipation of the FOMC meeting, with light unloading of swaps due to worries over narrowing interest rates differentials. \par \par \uc2  "If the FOMC meeting hikes short-term rates, the immediate impact could be felt on the swap rate because of the narrowing interest rate gap between the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," one said. \par \par \uc2  One-month swap was last at 15.50/16.25, two at 30.50/31.25, three at 46.25/47.00 and six at 95.50/96.00 points. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate at 2,313/2,505 and the conversion rate at 2,313/2,361 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds9o02jlj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
