\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Continues Up Vs. Dollar; Overseas Buyers \b0\par\par\uc2 223 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 1996\par 05:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-Dow Jones)--Indonesia's rupiah continues to strengthen versus the U.S. dollar in trading early Wednesday as overseas investors, attracted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's high yield, drive the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers note that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's wider \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band - introduced last week - combined with this bullish sentiment to the rupiah, could force the dollar down to the lower end of the new band over the next few weeks. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  early Wednesday left unchanged its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band at 2,310 rupiah - 2,502 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. unit is being bought at 2,320.50 rupiah in the spot market at 0301 GMT Wednesday, after starting the day at 2,321.50 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Traders see the dollar trading in a range between 2,319 rupiah and 2,322 rupiah through the rest of Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  'The market is still in love with the rupiah and its high yield,' stated a Singapore-based \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief. 'A downward trend for the dollar is likely barring any new political scares.' \par \par \uc2  Market players note, as well, that the rupiah has been supported recently by tightened liquidity in the market as well as a stronger performing stock market, though it is down Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-09-96 \par \par \uc2  0346GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds9i07iht\par }