\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah returns to favour with investors. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Raju Gopalakrishnan \par \uc2 594 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Sept 12 (Reuter) - The high-yielding Indonesian rupiah is once again returning to favour among emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's loosening of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah, which surged sharply against the dollar on Wednesday after Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  widened the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band to eight percent from five percent, ticked up slowly on Thursday and analysts saw more rises in coming months. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah jumped to 2,326 against the dollar on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement on Wednesday from an opening of 2,349 before settling back at about 2,330. On Thursday, it was trading at about 2,325.50/6.00 in the late afternoon. \par \par \uc2  "A lot of people are establishing outright positions," said Edwin Png, country treasurer at Bank of America. "A lot of hot money is coming in. Look at the problems in Thailand. Where else can you put your money? \par \par \uc2  "I thing the rupiah is still very attractive to foreign investors." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new band, which marks the perimeters outside of which it will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, was set at 2,309/2,501 on Wednesday and analysts said they saw the rate creeping to the lower end of the band by the end of the year. \par \par \uc2  "Right now, the market has room to play," said Jimmy Koh of the I.D.E.A. economic consultancy. "In the longer term, we see the rate heading back toward the lower end of the band. Perhaps by the end of the year. \par \par \uc2  "Further measures to liberalise rupiah movement and introduce a managed float can be expected over the medium term to avoid the problem of the spot rate converging with the lower end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band," Koh added. \par \par \uc2  "This merely reaffirms our preference for long rupiah positions, which now offer capital gains on top of a highly attractive (yield)." \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it widened the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band to contain the overheating economy and control capital inflows. \par \par \uc2  "It is an open question whether a wider band will be any more effective at slowing inflows (or curbing their effect) this time than in the past," said Peregrine Fixed Income in a commentary received by Reuters. "Unless the band is continuously widened, it has only a temporary effect. Nor have past band widenings appeared to have struck much fear into the hearts of foreign investors." \par \par \uc2  The rupiah has been in a continuous uptrend since the beginning of the year except for slight hiccups in June on unfounded rumours that President Suharto had suffered a heart attack and again in July when riots broke out in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  But sentiment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been restored after Suharto made a trip to Germany where doctors gave him a clean bill of health and the crackdown in the aftermath of the riots. \par \par \uc2  The strengthening, however, appears to have scuppered Bank Indonesia's stated target of depreciating the rupiah by five percent annually to help exports, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Peregrine estimated that the rupiah would need to depreciate at an annual rate of 8.15 percent from now until April 1 to achieve a four percent depreciation over the 1996-97 (April-March) fiscal year. \par \par \uc2  Koh said Indonesian authorities needed to look to other measures to boost exports. \par \par \uc2  "For the export side we believe the government will probably (need to) introduce more deregulation", he said. "Export competitiveness needs more than just a weakened rupiah. They've got to deal with the structural problem." \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds9c0386u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
