\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah stronger on bullish sentiment. \b0\par\par\uc2 394 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Sept 12 (Reuter) - Indonesia's rupiah strengthened against the dollar on sustained bullish sentiment in active late trading on Thursday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said selling of dollars by offshore and local players seemed to have pushed the rupiah up to Wednesday's high of around 2,326.0 level after the band widening. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was quoted at 2,325.75/26.25 at 0900 GMT, compared with an opening of 2,327.5/29.0. \par \par \uc2  "Overall sentiment remains bullish on the rupiah. But I'm a little bit confused over the present market trend," one Japanese bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He said operators were seen unloading six-month swap while buying three-month swap, giving a mixed picture over the short term direction and made it difficult to forecast the trend. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said the issue was also blurred by some uptrend of overnight dollar deposit rates to 5.625/5.75 percent. \par \par \uc2  "It's a bit difficult to draw a clear picture. I just go based on technical factors, whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is oversold or overbought. I just try to be a little bit faster," he said. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said operators were seen selling outright from the morning as the swap market was neglected during the hectic spot trading on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  One U.S. bank dealer said Singapore operators were seen taking profit from the swap market. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said spot rupiah was well resisted at the 2,329.0 level before it was broken to reach new strength. \par \par \uc2  He said operators were getting more cautious because the rate now was much more determined by market forces than by looking to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for direction. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday widened its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band to eight percent from five percent. \par \par \uc2  It also raised the minimum reserve requirement ratio to five percent from three percent effective April 16, 1997. \par \par \uc2  Overnight swap was at 0.35/0.45 and tom/next at 1.0/1.1. \par \par \uc2  One-month swap was quoted 14.75/15.75, two at 32.25/33.50, three at 47.50/48.25 and six at 97.00/98.25 points. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate at 2,309/2,501 and the conversion rate at 2,309/2,357 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds9c0382y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
