\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah/Exports -2: Exports Seen Weak In 1996 \b0\par\par\uc2 314 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 1996\par 13:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Though Indonesia's non-oil exports rose a respectable 13.2% to 10.155 billion rupiah in the first four months of 1996, Singh notes that that was partly due to an unusually low base in the first months of last year. \par \par \uc2  'Unless something drastic happens this year, 1996 figures in the second half are going to look bad,' Singh said. \par \par \uc2  By late Friday, the rupiah has depreciated 2.5% from the start of the year - when the dollar traded at 2,283.50 rupiah - more of less in line with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  annual depreciation target. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  adjusts its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - which currently ranges from 2,329 rupiah to 2,447 rupiah - in order to ensure a steady depreciation that is designed to bolster exports. \par \par \uc2  Analysts also note that Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to widen its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band in June worked in its favor this week. It ensured that even with political uncertainty, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained well inside the band without the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile the Bank of Thailand has been forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily this week to defend its less flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg for the Thai baht. \par \par \uc2  In July, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  widened the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band to 118 rupiah from 66 rupiah as part of a consistent policy of giving the market a greater say in setting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value. \par \par \uc2  'The rupiah has now caught up with a 5% depreciation against the dollar, and despite the political tensions, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has never needed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The market has taken care of things on its own.' says Dominique Maire, a regional economist at the Union Bank of Switzerland in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Even with the latest shocks, the rupiah remains near the stronger end of the band.< \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 02-08-96 \par \par \uc2  1106GMT \par \par \uc2  1137 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds8206gqd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
