\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia's Rupiah -2: Overnight JIBOR At 13% \b0\par\par\uc2 182 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 1996\par 05:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia, the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , injected 294 billion rupiah in net liquidity into the money market early Thursday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The expiration of Bank Indonesia certificates, Sertifikat Bank Indonesia (SBI), added 835 billion rupiah into the system. However, the expiration of the money market certificates, Surat Berharga Pasar Uang (SBPU), absorbed back 141 billion rupiah, in addition to 400 billion rupiah through the settlement of new SBIs. \par \par \uc2  The overnight Jakarta Interbank Offered Rates (JIBOR) early Thursday fell slightly to 13% from 14.5% Wednesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the premium of the dollar-rupiah swaps early Thursday slid to 0.55/0.60 from 0.60/0.65 Wednesday, dealers added. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia left unchanged its dollar-rupiah indication rate at 2,324 rupiah - 2,370 rupiah, and its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band at 2,324 rupiah - 2,442 rupiah. Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Wednesday cut both the indication rate and trading band by one rupiah following the dollar's slide against the other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-07-96 \par \par \uc2  0359GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds7i05vek\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
